{"ticker":"financial","name":"Financial","exchange":"","sector":"","generatedAt":"2026-10-20T15:22:30.249Z","posts":[{"id":"tradingqna-tqna-543289","source":"tradingqna","author":"cvs","handle":"@cvs","community":"TradingQnA","timestamp":"2026-10-16T07:39:41.577Z","text":"Financial gift for my parents — Yes. Filing ITR is not having to pay taxes though. Filing an ITR is a good idea to avoid complication in future (however unlikely they maybe for relatively small amounts). Also execute a Gift-deed. Costs a couple hundred bucks to get it notarised. But definitely helps with peace of mind.","url":"https://tradingqna.com/t/financial-gift-for-my-parents/34753/5","sentiment":"bearish","likes":1,"comments":0,"firstSeenAt":"2026-10-16T09:47:42.217Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-10-19T17:31:09.167Z"},{"id":"tradingqna-tqna-543284","source":"tradingqna","author":"Bharat","handle":"@Bharat","community":"TradingQnA","timestamp":"2026-10-16T07:10:24.876Z","text":"Financial gift for my parents — If I gift money to my mother to her savings account. Does she have to file ITR ? She is a housewife does not have any income. She only has one savings account where AMB is 25000 so she only receives 2.5 percent interest per annum. if gift amount cross 2.5 lacs in single financial year. Does she have to file ITR ?","url":"https://tradingqna.com/t/financial-gift-for-my-parents/34753/4","sentiment":"neutral","likes":0,"comments":1,"firstSeenAt":"2026-10-16T09:47:42.217Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-10-19T17:31:09.167Z"},{"id":"news-gn-RlQ3d2VzMms3MFBLYUV1a3Mwc0tMaDVB","source":"news","author":"The Motley Fool","handle":"The Motley Fool","community":"Google News","timestamp":"2026-10-13T22:30:00.000Z","text":"2 Financial Stocks to Buy That Berkshire Hathaway Kept While Selling Visa and Mastercard","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxQU0RoTXhyWU5EXzhBMkdxZHZRUGRMR2lYSXFIMVFrVjVlZHM2VXREWHVFYUpNS2pHVkRMb1lwY2ZXRGNuVXBnMjVRTDkyc1hCRTFYNXZSXzc4RExWOGN1Z3JLRHVEa0tkdFVIbk9hMmlUUV92RGVKZFY0anhhdlJXRlQ3d2VzMms3MFBLYUV1a3Mwc0tMaDVB?oc=5","sentiment":"neutral","likes":0,"comments":0,"firstSeenAt":"2026-10-14T00:37:12.805Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-10-14T00:37:12.805Z"},{"id":"news-gn-pmbXhyLUd5TGx3S1RhejJlWmFHRlhsUQ","source":"news","author":"Yahoo Finance","handle":"Yahoo Finance","community":"Google News","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:50:00.000Z","text":"2 Financial Stocks to Buy That Berkshire Hathaway Kept While Selling Visa and Mastercard","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxPUnd1Wi00dDRnaEhFN3BpS05ON2JIQkdFTkRwVWsyN3BCM2M0bFFwdFd0V0pjai1WMVBwYnRfQWNvcldXeHVxU0ItM2FwazRSZi1JMy1zN2NUWXBVWkh6eEZzVGhOV2F2YzZZVTFpb0JpQ0JyQWctaXdkeGhTdW1sZ0JYVHpqV1pmbXhyLUd5TGx3S1RhejJlWmFHRlhsUQ?oc=5","sentiment":"neutral","likes":0,"comments":0,"firstSeenAt":"2026-10-14T05:24:58.832Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-10-16T09:47:42.217Z"},{"id":"tradingqna-tqna-542725","source":"tradingqna","author":"DishantSR","handle":"@DishantSR","community":"TradingQnA","timestamp":"2026-10-13T04:18:32.983Z","text":"Financial ratios for Banking sector evaluation — Adding to neha’s list, a few more that matter specifically for private vs PSU comparisons: ROA and ROE : ROA (around 1% is decent for a bank) is the cleaner comparison, since banks run on high leverage and ROE alone can flatter a thinly capitalised bank. Cost-to-income ratio : operating expenses / net total income. Private banks usually run leaner; PSU banks carry higher staff and pension costs. Provision coverage ratio (PCR) : how much of the gross NPA is already provided for. Two banks with the same GNPA can look very different once you check…","url":"https://tradingqna.com/t/financial-ratios-for-banking-sector-evaluation/198753/3","sentiment":"neutral","likes":2,"comments":0,"firstSeenAt":"2026-10-13T08:27:33.413Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-10-19T17:31:09.167Z"},{"id":"tradingqna-tqna-542671","source":"tradingqna","author":"neha1101","handle":"@neha1101","community":"TradingQnA","timestamp":"2026-10-12T13:22:16.529Z","text":"Finan